# Odoo.sh Staging Environment

**Effective:** 2026-08-07

## SSH SSOT (mandatory)

Live Connect credentials live in **repo-root `.env.local`** (gitignored):

| Key | Format |
|---|---|
| `ODOO_SH_STAGING_SSH` | `BUILD_ID@cryptoxdog-ib-odoo-19-staging-BUILD_ID.dev.odoo.com` |
| `ODOO_SH_STAGING_URL` | `https://cryptoxdog-ib-odoo-19-staging-BUILD_ID.dev.odoo.com/odoo` |
| `ODOO_SH_STAGING_BRANCH` | `Staging` |

**Canonical connect (agents + operators):**

```bash
set -a && source .env.local && set +a
ssh "$ODOO_SH_STAGING_SSH"
```

Rules:

1. **Never** put a literal `ssh ` prefix inside `ODOO_SH_STAGING_SSH` (breaks `ssh "$ODOO_SH_STAGING_SSH"`).
2. Odoo.sh **rotates build IDs** on every Staging rebuild — update `.env.local` from the Connect dropdown first; this rule's snapshot below is secondary.
3. Project SSH **key** is stable (Odoo.sh Profile); only the build number/host changes.
4. After a rebuild: update `.env.local` → optionally sync the snapshot table in this file → diagnose via `plasticos-odoo-sh-deploy`.

## Staging instance (snapshot — may lag `.env.local`)

| Property | Value |
|---|---|
| URL | `https://cryptoxdog-ib-odoo-19-staging-36099032.dev.odoo.com` |
| Build ID | `36099032` |
| Branch | `Staging` |
| Platform | Odoo.sh |

## Shell commands

```bash
set -a && source .env.local && set +a
BID="${ODOO_SH_STAGING_SSH%%@*}"
ssh "$ODOO_SH_STAGING_SSH" "odoo-bin shell -d cryptoxdog-ib-odoo-19-staging-${BID}"
```

## Web lead staging endpoints

| Method | Path | Auth |
|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/api/v1/web-lead` | Bearer token |
| `POST` | `/api/v1/cognito-webhook` | Bearer token |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/web-lead/health` | None |

## Deployment boundary

- A push to `Staging` triggers an Odoo.sh deployment.
- Commit and push both require explicit operator authorization.
- SSH sessions are ephemeral; changes outside persistent storage are lost on rebuild.
